---
// Foundations
import Button from "@/components/fundations/elements/Button.astro";
import Wrapper from "@/components/fundations/containers/Wrapper.astro";
---

<section class="bg-gradient-to-b from-base-100 to-white">
  <Wrapper variant="standard" class="py-16 lg:py-24">
    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-base-300 bg-base-950 shadow-2xl ring-1 ring-base-950/10">
      <div class="grid gap-0 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,0.95fr)_minmax(320px,0.55fr)]">
        <div class="p-8 sm:p-10 lg:p-14">
          <p class="border-l border-accent-500 pl-4 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-base-300">
            AI Governance & Retention Risk
          </p>

          <h2 class="mt-8 max-w-4xl font-display text-3xl font-medium uppercase leading-[1.05] tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl">
            AI is increasing workload for the people your organization can least afford to lose.
          </h2>

          <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-base leading-8 text-base-200 sm:text-lg">
            The Power User Trap℠ begins when high performers become the informal validation layer for AI adoption. They learn the tools first, troubleshoot failures, verify outputs, train colleagues, and absorb the cognitive burden while standard productivity metrics show improvement.
          </p>

          <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-base leading-8 text-base-200 sm:text-lg">
            The organization sees adoption. It does not see the concentration of oversight work. By the time the exit appears in retention data, the implementation capacity has already left.
          </p>

          <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row">
            <Button
              isLink
              href="/invisible-attrition/power-user-trap"
              variant="accent"
              size="xs"
            >
              Read the Power User Trap℠
            </Button>

            <Button
              isLink
              href="/request-briefing"
              variant="secondary"
              size="xs"
            >
              Request Briefing
            </Button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <aside class="border-t border-white/10 bg-white/[0.04] p-8 sm:p-10 lg:border-l lg:border-t-0 lg:p-10">
          <p class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent-300">
            What your data misses
          </p>

          <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5">
            <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.04] p-5">
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-white">
                Oversight burden
              </p>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-base-300">
                The work of checking, correcting, and validating AI output concentrates in the employees already trusted to exercise judgment.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.04] p-5">
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-white">
                Invisible implementation work
              </p>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-base-300">
                Training colleagues, troubleshooting tools, and maintaining workflow quality often sit outside job descriptions, workload models, and compensation decisions.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-2xl border border-accent-400/70 bg-accent-500/10 p-5">
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-white">
                Retention exposure
              </p>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-base-200">
                Productivity appears to rise while leadership capacity erodes. The risk becomes visible only after the person exits.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Wrapper>
</section>
